{"author":{"id":"7c5527b9befade3b1be0c1d677ac996815288d8332f34269730a5b81425ee5be"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791208846,"nonce":"K0rERAYSHBUqAfseOwBevI6fEAA=","metadata":{"github-url":"https://github.com/EPFL-ENAC/vps-mitsi/issues/38","origin":"github","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"I_kwDOULtcMc8AAAABVIseHQ","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:labels":"","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:number":"38","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:status":"open","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:text":"84d27c3a2a7e3c8cb255f340d958f4dccd845019ffe6d840e7d03c8b5ff5cd77","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:title":"[CHORE](Deployment) Remove the Kubernetes deploy workflow, GitHub Pages is the target","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:url":"https://github.com/EPFL-ENAC/vps-mitsi/issues/38"},"title":"[CHORE](Deployment) Remove the Kubernetes deploy workflow, GitHub Pages is the target","message":"**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**\nMITSI currently has two production targets:\n\n- `.github/workflows/pages.yml` publishes `main` to GitHub Pages (#4).\n- `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` builds a Docker image and deploys `dev`, `stage` and `v*.*.*` tags to the ENAC Kubernetes cluster through `EPFL-ENAC/epfl-enac-build-push-deploy-action@v3.1.0`.\n\nWe deploy to GitHub Pages, so the Kubernetes path is dead weight:\n\n- It builds and pushes an image on every push to `dev` and needs the `CD_TOKEN` secret.\n- It keeps `frontend/Dockerfile`, `nginx.conf` and `entrypoint.sh` alive.\n- It triggers on `stage`, a branch that doesn't exist.\n- The READMEs describe a `dev` → `stage` → `main` flow that doesn't match what we do: #26 merged `dev` straight into `main`.\n\n**Describe the solution you'd like**\n- [ ] Record in #31 that GitHub Pages is the only production target.\n- [ ] Delete `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`.\n- [ ] Decide what happens to `frontend/Dockerfile`, `frontend/nginx.conf` and `frontend/entrypoint.sh`:\n  - delete them (git history keeps them if we ever need them again), **or**\n  - keep them on purpose for local container use, and clean them up as described in the build-cleanup issue.\n- [ ] Ask ENAC-IT to remove the `epfl-vps/mitsi` overlays in `enack8s-app-config` and the running `dev` deployment, and delete the published `ghcr.io` images.\n- [ ] Update the \"Deployment\" section of the root `README.md` and \"Production builds\" in `frontend/README.md`.\n- [ ] Define the Pages release flow. Today every push to `main` publishes. Do the `v0.1.0` and `v0.1.1` tags still mean anything? Is `stage` coming back?\n\n**Describe alternatives you've considered**\nKeep Kubernetes as production and drop Pages. This contradicts #4 and the direction of #31.\n\n**Additional context**\nRaised in an architecture review of `dev` at `b35fc8c`. Image vulnerability scanning in the CI issue only applies if the Docker path is kept.","files":null}]}